3. Parameterize the API endpoint
The endpoint is already parameterized using ${endpoint} from the CSV file.

For example:
CSV variable	   HTTP Request setting
${endpoint}	     Server Name or IP
${username}	     Email in the request body
${password}    	Password in the request body

4. Extract a session token and reuse it
For a mock login API that returns JSON containing a token, add a Regular Expression Extractor under the login HTTP Request:

Right-click login request → Add → Post Processors → Regular Expression Extractor.

Configure:
Setting	Value
Name	Extract Session Token
Apply to	Main sample only
Field to check	Body
Reference Name	sessionToken
Regular Expression	"token"\s*:\s*"([^"]+)"
Template	$1$
Match No.	1
Default Value	TOKEN_NOT_FOUND

If the login response contains {"token":"abc123"}, JMeter stores abc123 in ${sessionToken}.

